message: "If you use these certificates, the checker or the search code, please cite this work."
title: "Simple symmetric Venn diagrams with 17, 19 and 23 curves"
authors:
  - family-names: Dzoba
    given-names: Chris
date-released: 2026-10-06
version: "1.3"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dzoba/venn17"
url: "https://github.com/dzoba/venn17"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Venn diagram
  - symmetric
  - combinatorics
  - certificate
abstract: >-
  Simple, rotationally symmetric Venn diagrams with 17 curves, with 19 curves and with 23 curves, the
  smallest open cases since the 11- and 13-curve diagrams of Mamakani and Ruskey (2014),
  given as machine-checkable certificates, one 17-curve and one 19-curve certificate verified in
  Lean 4, together with a standalone checker, the search program that found them, a plotter and the
  write-up. The five 23-curve certificates (889 MB each) are carried as release assets and in the
  Zenodo archive rather than in the git tree. Also includes the first non-monotone simple symmetric
  Venn diagrams with 11 and 13 curves.
